WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.340
Quick question. Would you walk into court with the
other side's lawyer? No? Then why do most

00:05.340 --> 00:10.060
businesses sign a lease with the landlord's agent?
At Your Office Space, that's exactly what tenant

00:10.060 --> 00:15.720
representation fixes. A tenant rep is a property
advisor who works only for you, not the landlord,

00:16.020 --> 00:21.480
not the vendor, just you. Here's what we do. One, we
work out what your business actually needs.

00:21.960 --> 00:27.140
Two, we search the whole market, including the half
that never gets listed. Three, we compare

00:27.140 --> 00:33.820
deals on what you'll really pay, not the headline
rent. Four, we negotiate. Rent, incentives, reviews,

00:34.260 --> 00:41.240
make good, the lot. Five, we work with your
solicitor so it all lands in the lease. And it adds
up. On a

00:41.240 --> 00:49.900
$100,000 lease, one CPI review clause cost a tenant
$25,500 over five years. That's one line. So why

00:49.900 --> 00:54.660
do most business owners only call us when it's too
late? Because the problems don't show up on day one,

00:54.660 --> 00:59.380
they show up years later. A rent review that
compounds. A make good bill on the way out.

00:59.840 --> 01:05.500
An option window that quietly closes. By then, the
deal's done. Start 12 to 18 months before your

01:05.500 --> 01:10.960
lease ends. That's when you've got options. And
leverage. Leasing, renewing or buying, we're on

01:10.960 --> 01:16.460
your side. And when the lease is signed, we can look
after the fit out, furniture and cleaning too.

01:16.460 --> 01:19.300
Your Office Space. Book a clarity call.
